{
  "heading": "The Solar System (and how to colonize it within the next few centuries)",
  "cueText": "The Solar System has the Sun as its gravitational centre (or more specifically the common center of mass of all objects within the system)\n\n8 planets, at least 5 dwarf planets, hundreds of moons, millions of minor planets and objects\n\nDepicted is the map of mostly all main rounded bodies (except for a few notable moons), which is the Sun, the 8 rounded planets, the key dwarf planets, and all rounded moons (asides from a few)\n\nWe live on planet Earth, and the moon is the next space goal for colonization thanks to the Artemis program\n\nNext is Mars itself, then one of Jupiter's moons (mainly Callisto because of Jupiter's radiation), then Titan (because of its thick atmosphere)\n\nMercury is too hot, Venus is too hot and acidic\n\nWe cannot land on the giant planets, we have to use its moons as landed bases\n\nThe far out dwarf planets could be used in the far future for colonies, bases and resource mines",
  "summary": "Projected colonisation path (for surface landed bases): The Moon, Mars, and beyond (which will be most likely Callisto, then Titan), and then other moons of the outer solar system. Cloud cities are also theoretically possible on Venus and the Giants but they are difficult than landed bases",
